# Line endings are pinned to LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# This overrides core.autocrlf, which is commonly set to `true` on Windows. Without it, a Windows
# checkout gets CRLF in the working tree and `.editorconfig`'s `end_of_line = lf` fails the
# `dotnet format --verify-no-changes` gate locally while passing on Linux CI — the worst kind of
# difference, because it only shows up on one developer's machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only shell scripts must keep CRLF to run.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary assets are never normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.snk binary
*.pfx binary

# Lockfiles are generated; keeping them diffable as text is useful, but a merge conflict in one
# should be resolved by regenerating rather than by hand.
package-lock.json text
packages.lock.json text
